  <text>
    <body>
      <div>
        <head>In the directories</head>
        <p>Francis E. Striezel, art carver, is listed at No. 29 <ref target="civic?id=Madeline%20Street">Madeline Street</ref> in 1900. In 1905 and 1910 F. E. Striezel is at No. 51, a pattern carver, then an art and pattern carver.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <head>On the electoral roll</head>
        <p>Francis Edmond Striezel, art carver, is on the 1905 <ref target="civic?id=Electoral-Rolls">electoral roll</ref> at 51 Madeline Street, with Clara Natalia Striezel, home duties.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <head>Neighbours</head>
        <p>In 1900 G. Williamson, tailor, is at No. 27 and Fredk. J. Steabben, confectioner, at No. 31. At No. 51 his neighbours are <ref target="civic?id=Carl%20Fischer">Carl Fischer</ref>, hairdresser and tobacconist, and John Morgan, fishmonger, in 1905, and A. Kenrick, hairdresser, in 1910.</p>
      </div>
